Watch-validation rows now say where they came from, and the outcome lives only in severity. Committed as 09640667. Build, the full test suite, clippy with -D warnings and the fmt check all pass.

What was wrong: auto_validate_after_failure_to always wrote trigger: "watch_failure", including after a green watch cycle. So every watch row claimed a failure whatever actually happened. The planner counted 76 rows that say watch_failure in trigger but watch_success in severity; I didn't recount them. The cli and ci_harvest writers already follow the rule this breaks: trigger names the source and severity names the outcome.

Changes:
• **Fix (src/commands_risk_snapshots.rs):** the path now writes trigger: "watch". I updated the doc comments to state the source/outcome rule.
• Tests:
  • New test test_auto_validate_trigger_is_source_not_outcome. It runs the real writer through the existing temp-directory seam, once with watch_success and once with watch_failure, and checks that trigger is "watch" both times and severity matches what was passed in.
  • The existing exact check in test_auto_validate_with_synthetic_snapshot now expects "watch". It's still an exact match, not a looser one.
• **Tests failed before the fix:** before the fix both tests failed, on the trigger value.
• **Positive control:** in one command, I put `"watch_failure"` back with a `NEUTERED` marker. Both tests failed by name. I then restored the line and they passed again. Afterwards NEUTERED appears 0 times in the file.
• **`ARCHITECTURE.md:** the "Open, not fixed here" line now says the defect is fixed. It warns that rows written before this commit say watch_failure for both outcomes, so their outcome has to be read from severity`. Old rows are left unchanged because the ledger is append-only.

No counts or verdicts changed. Before editing I searched src/ and scripts/. Nothing in production reads the trigger string; it appears only in the writer and in test data. (scripts/skill_evolve_report.py reads a field called trigger, but from a different file.)

File size: the size gate printed that commands_risk_snapshots.rs "grew to 2258 lines, 78 past its recorded 2180". That leaves 22 lines of the 100-line allowance, so the next small change to this file could fail the gate. The net addition was 24 lines, under the task's ~40 limit. I copied the printed message into the comment in tests/module_size.rs and left the recorded size at 2180, since this is a warning and not a failure.

One thing outside this task: the same gate also warns that src/commands_risk.rs is 1 line over its recorded 6601. I didn't touch that file or its entry.
